  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the given figure the magnetic flux through the loop increases according to the relation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#981;</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>t</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#981;</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math> is in milliwebers and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math>&nbsp;is in seconds. The magnitude of current through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> resistor at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mA</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/249963bb-0e18-4476-bc96-6ef1ed150131-image.png\" style=\"width: 287px; height: 193px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
